## WHO-UMC Causality Assessment

* Classification: Probable / Likely
* Rationale:
  1. Temporal Sequence: Onset occurred 4 months after drug initiation, matching the known delayed presentation latency characteristic of ACE-inhibitor angioedema.
  2. De-challenge: Mucosal swelling completely subsided following drug cessation and supportive care.
  3. Exclusion of Alternatives: Normal C1 esterase inhibitor levels ruled out hereditary angioedema, and absence of urticaria/elevated tryptase excluded classic IgE-mediated allergy.
  4. Re-challenge: Re-exposure was ethically avoided due to life-threatening airway compromise, placing causality in Probable under WHO criteria rather than Certain.

